  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "For starters, I can understand the benefits of having Group Public Instances (GPI). Creating an open group community, a get-together, or even host events and allow anyone to join. However, an issue that is happening that should be discussed or fixed, is the moderation tools available in said GPIs. I shouldn't have to experience going into a world, such as the Black Cat, and randomly get kicked.\n\nAs an example, a group of people; myself, and friends all started randomly getting kicked because someone thought it'd be a \"funny\" moment because they have that power.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-zAkYgTBB1c\n\nI'm not saying that there shouldn't be moderation tools available for group members but there should be better limits to prevent false use the moderation tools if it's a GPI.",
